cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Kuiva in published work, please cite it as below, and cite the methods and basis sets it implements as listed in the References section of README.md."
title: "Kuiva: relativistic multireference quantum chemistry"
abstract: >-
  Two-component (X2C) relativistic multireference quantum chemistry for strongly
  correlated, strongly relativistic systems. Spin-orbit coupling is introduced at
  the CASSCF/CI level, with two-electron spin-orbit coupling by atomic mean-field
  X2C; the CI step is solved by conventional complex determinant CI or by an
  in-house tree tensor network (DMRG/TTNS), and dynamic correlation by strongly
  contracted NEVPT2.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mansikkamäki"
    given-names: "Akseli"
version: 0.27.0
date-released: "2026-08-13"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mansikkamaki/kuiva"
keywords:
  - quantum chemistry
  - relativistic quantum chemistry
  - X2C
  - spin-orbit coupling
  - multireference
  - CASSCF
  - NEVPT2
  - DMRG
  - tensor networks
  - single-molecule magnets
